Development Phases (Left Side):

    Requirements Analysis

        Gather and analyze user and system requirements.

        Define what the system should do, its constraints, and overall goals.

        Output: Requirements Specification Document.

    System Design

        Translate requirements into a system architecture.

        Define system components, modules, interfaces, and data flow.

        Output: System Design Document.

    Architectural Design (High-Level Design)

        Break down the system into smaller subsystems or modules.

        Define relationships between modules and how they interact.

        Output: High-Level Design Document.

    Module Design (Low-Level Design)

        Design the internal logic of each module.

        Specify algorithms, data structures, and detailed module specifications.

        Output: Low-Level Design Document.

    Coding / Implementation

        Write the actual code based on module designs.

        Implement modules as per specifications.

Testing Phases (Right Side):

    Unit Testing

        Test individual modules for correctness.

        Verify that each module performs as expected in isolation.

    Integration Testing

        Test combined modules and their interactions.

        Verify interfaces and data flow between modules.

    System Testing

        Test the complete integrated system.

        Validate the system’s compliance with specified requirements.

    Acceptance Testing

        Conducted by the end user or client.

        Validate the system in the real-world environment against user needs and requirements.

